# INVWINSQ.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: the split
# view's menus and commands.  The Record menu, from the menu bar and as
# the pop-up, is the tree's while the tree has the focus, with Next
# pane, and the contents' once TAB has moved the focus there.  CTRL-D
# in the contents duplicates Office's last item, Box B2's drives, the
# contents loaded again with the copy and the panel counting it.
# Locations > New location from the contents gives the tree the focus
# first, which shows the location added, selected, beside its empty
# contents.  A letter seeks Shelf A1 in the tree, its contents loaded;
# CTRL-E renames it, the tree loaded again while the contents keep the
# old name in their Location column, until Reindex loads both, though
# TAB into them counts them under the new name at once.  At level 1 the
# tree's entries that change a location are grayed, but not Next pane,
# which TAB still does, and the contents' Record menu grays its own.
# The end by Exit.  TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINSQ.SNP is its snapshot;
# TEST/splitchk.py checks it.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER ALT-L B
S LOCS
K ALT-C
S TREEMENU
K ESC ESC SHIFT-F10
S TREEPOP
K ESC TAB ALT-C
S CMENU
K ESC ESC SHIFT-F10
S CPOP
K ESC END CTRL-D ENTER
S COPIED
K ALT-L N
S NEWDLG
T Lab
K ALT-C
T LAB
K ENTER
S NEWLOC
K HOME
T S
S SEEK
K CTRL-E
T Shelf Z9
K ENTER
S RENAMED
K TAB
S RENPANE
K ESC
K ALT-A I
S REINDEX
K ENTER
S REINDEXD
K ALT-F L STAB
T READER
K TAB
T Reader1986
K ENTER ALT-L B
S RLOCS
K TAB
S RPANE
K ALT-F X
